[101.979803, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Month arithmetic incorrectly capped every anchor at day 28, and cycle\n  iteration drifted from the original anchor. Renewals now clamp to the actual\n  target month end and recover the original anchor day, including leap days.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan at the\n  change-date price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at the\n  cycle start; new-plan prices are selected on the change date.\n- Monthly/annual switches now charge a full new interval and re-anchor on the\n  change date. Invoice line periods reflect the separate old and new cycles.\n- Rounding now uses exact rational half-even rounding, independent of Decimal\n  precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\nAdded regression coverage for late-month boundaries, leap/century years,\nactual cycle lengths, exact rounding, price dates, invoice lines, CLI previews,\nand renewal schedules after re-anchoring. Existing tests and financial"]
[101.980052, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff"]
[101.980066, "i", " data\nwere not altered.\n\n## Validation and release blocker\n\nAll finance worked examples and billing/calendar regressions pass. CLI checks\ninclude the month-end invoice (2,321 cents due), leap-day annual downgrade\n(-19,508-cent subtotal; 22,008 cents carried including the existing balance),\nand monthly-to-annual switch (11,831 cents due).\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 28 tests with **one error**:\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\nThis error was also present in the baseline. `data/subscriptions.json` references\nP-31 on sub_1151, but `data/partners.json` has only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No P-31\ncontract/rate definition was found elsewhere in the repository.\n\n**Release remains blocked.** Obtain P-31's authoritative contracted commission\nrate and add its approved partner record (or have the data owner correct the\nsubscription reference if it is erroneous), then rerun the full suite. No rate\nwas invented, no customer record was removed, and no test was bypass"]
[101.980074, "i", "ed to make\nthe release gate green.\nEOF\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[101.980268, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.980331, "o", "## Fixed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.981101, "o", "- Month arithmetic incorrectly capped every anchor at day 28, and cycle\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[101.98114, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.982025, "o", "  iteration drifted from the original anchor. Renewals now clamp to the actual\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   target month end and recover the original anchor day, including leap days.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   change-date price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   cycle start; new-plan prices are selected on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.982223, "o", "- Monthly/annual switches now charge a full new interval and re-anchor on the"]
[101.982336, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.982503, "o", "  change date. Invoice line periods reflect the separate old and new cycles.\r\n"]
[101.982607, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.983136, "o", "- Rounding now uses exact rational half-even rounding, independent of Decimal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Added regression coverage for late-month boundaries, leap/century years,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> actual cycle lengths, exact rounding, price dates, invoice lines, CLI previews,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[101.983479, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.983713, "o", "and renewal schedules after re-anchoring. Existing tests and financial data\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.983786, "o", "were not altered.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Validation and release blocker\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[101.983851, "o", "All finance worked examples and billing/calendar regressions pass. CLI checks\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[101.983998, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
